<title>USA: Koch raises U.S. posted crude prices 25 cts/bbl.</title>
<headline>Koch raises U.S. posted crude prices 25 cts/bbl.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1997-07-01</dateline>
<text>
<p>Koch Oil Co, a unit of Koch Industries, said it raised the the price it will pay for U.S. crude oil by 25 cents, effective Tuesday.</p>
<p>The increase brings the new price for U.S. benchmark grade West Texas Intermediate to $18.00 a barrel and West Texas Sour to $15.25 a barrel.</p>
<p>Light Louisiana sweet crude is now $17.50 and Oklahoma sweet is $18.00.</p>
<p>--New York Oil Desk, +1 212 859 1623</p>
</text>
